          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Are there eating habits that tend to make reflux worse?",
          "answer": "The sources I searched don't say which eating habits make reflux worse, so I can't give you a list from them.\n\nTwo points touch on the topic. The general GERD reference (condition-gerd) explains that reflux often happens when the muscle ring between the esophagus and stomach relaxes at the wrong time. The GERD guideline (guideline-gerd-initial-management-and-alarm-features) says that when treatment doesn't work, a clinician first checks how it is timed relative to meals. That suggests meal timing can matter, but the passage doesn't say which foods or meal patterns to change.\n\nA clinician or dietitian can look at your own eating pattern and suggest changes. Separately from these sources, and as general advice only: if your reflux is severe, keeps getting worse, or comes with trouble swallowing, weight loss, vomiting blood, or black stools, get medical care promptly.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
